From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 15:18:50 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 010/230] Fix standings goal difference: read goals from the v2
 standings feed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The daily standings sync pulled ESPN's per-match summary feed, whose
standings block only publishes games played / W / D / L / points / rank.
pointsFor and pointsAgainst never arrive, so goals_for and goals_against
stayed NULL and the GD column rendered as 0 for every club.

Switch the sync, the CLI backfill and the normalizer to ESPN's v2
/api/v2/sports/soccer/{league}/standings?season=YYYY endpoint, which
publishes the full stat set. All ESPN shape knowledge stays in
normalize.ts: it now accepts both the v2 children[].standings.entries
shape and the legacy summary groups[] shape, since entry.team is a real
object on one and a bare name string on the other.

Re-syncing clears the nulls (96 → 0 across 11 domestic leagues) and the
GD column now matches ESPN exactly.

